WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:08.467
Welcome to season three
of<i> 13 Reasons Why.</i>

2
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.760
If you've been watching.

3
00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:13.353
you know our show portrays a number
of real issues facing teenagers today.

4
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.810
We tell stories about things
like substance abuse.

5
00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:19.101
bullying. sexual assault.
violence and suicide.

6
00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:22.976
If these issues are in your life.
this series may not be right for you.

7
00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:24.975
Or you may not want to watch it alone.

8
00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.687
So. watch with your parents.
your family or your friends.

9
00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:29.608
Then talk to someone about what you see...

10
00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.736
What you think about it.
How it makes you feel.

11
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.530
And if you find you need help.

12
00:00:33.742 --> 00:00:35.082
talk to a trusted adult.

13
00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:36.619
Like a school counselor.

14
00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.253
Or call a local helpline

15
00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.170
or visit our website
at 13ReasonsWhy.info.

16
00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:44.292
Once you start talking about it.
it gets better.

17
00:00:44.962 --> 00:00:45.802
Enjoy the show.

18
00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.089
Enjoy the conversation.

19
00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:48.632
And take care of each other.

20
00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:05.107
[theme music playing]

21
00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:31.053
<i>My name is Amorowat Anysia Achola.</i>

22
00:01:31.717 --> 00:01:33.137
<i>You can call me Ani.</i>

23
00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:41.139
<i>I'm a senior at Liberty High School.</i>

24
00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:43.056
You were lying to me the whole time.

25
00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:48.899
[Bryce] Goddammit. Ani. I need you!
I need you so fucking bad.

26
00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:57.908
[woman] Amorowat?

27
00:02:09.296 --> 00:02:11.046
[Ani]<i> My mum's a home health care worker.</i>

28
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.844
<i>We just got to Evergreen last spring.
April.</i>

29
00:02:14.092 --> 00:02:15.892
[Ani] Right. I'm off then.

30
00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:17.345
[Ani's mum] Wait...

31
00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:20.139
This is fashion?

32
00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:23.103
It is quite stylish. yes. Thank you.

33
00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:26.265
- The things that school allows.
- You don't even know.

34
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:30.317
I didn't see you all weekend.
I had both days off.

35
00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:33.029
I had projects.

36
00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:36.275
Next Sunday. I'll go to church with you.

37
00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:37.815
- Yes?
- At the very least.

38
00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:51.462
["Regret" playing]

39
00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.018
[Ani]<i> I just started at Liberty in April.</i>

40
00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.361
<i>About eight months ago.</i>

41
00:03:10.649 --> 00:03:12.479
<i>Yeah. I'm the new girl.</i>

42
00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:15.951
<i>Do I like Liberty?</i>

43
00:03:17.364 --> 00:03:18.364
<i>Sure.</i>

44
00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:20.826
<i>It's an... interesting place.</i>

45
00:03:23.954 --> 00:03:26.794
<i>Stuff happens at Liberty High School.
you know?</i>

46
00:03:29.543 --> 00:03:32.843
<i>♪ I would like a place I can call my own ♪</i>

47
00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:36.341
<i>♪ Have a conversation on the telephone ♪</i>

48
00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:38.885
[Ani]<i> I'm guessing that's why I'm here.</i>

49
00:03:40.846 --> 00:03:44.016
<i>♪ I would not complain
Of my wounded heart ♪</i>

50
00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:46.519
[Ani]<i> You think I know something</i>
<i>about what happened?</i>

51
00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:51.188
Well. I do.

52
00:03:51.857 --> 00:03:54.817
<i>♪ I would like a place
I could call my own ♪</i>

53
00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:58.735
<i>♪ Have a conversation on the telephone ♪</i>

54
00:03:59.156 --> 00:04:01.366
[Ani]<i> I'm sure you got pieces</i>
<i>from other people.</i>

55
00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:06.288
<i>♪ I would not complain
Of my wounded heart ♪</i>

56
00:04:08.165 --> 00:04:09.955
<i>I can help you put them together.</i>

57
00:04:11.293 --> 00:04:12.793
[song fades]

58
00:04:13.003 --> 00:04:13.843
[Ani] Jess...

59
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.040
If you're gonna apologize
about the homecoming game...

60
00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.089
The police took Clay.

61
00:04:17.841 --> 00:04:20.221
- What?
- Just now. I saw them out front.

62
00:04:20.302 --> 00:04:22.052
Shit! Why now?

63
00:04:22.137 --> 00:04:24.427
It's November.
Spring Fling was last April.

64
00:04:25.724 --> 00:04:26.894
And why Clay?

65
00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.330
[police radio]<i> All units in the vicinity</i>
<i>of Mission and Twelfth.</i>

66
00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:32.354
<i>assault in progress.</i>

67
00:04:32.564 --> 00:04:35.074
<i>1705 Mission. Please respond.</i>

68
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:36.395
Wanna get that?

69
00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:38.245
- I'll take him back to the station.
- Right.

70
00:04:38.361 --> 00:04:41.451
Dispatch. Unit 12 is responding.
Unit 4 returning to station.

71
00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:44.449
[police radio]
<i>683. that's one. seven. zero...</i>

72
00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:45.994
[police siren]

73
00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:47.788
[tires screeching]

74
00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:50.792
[sirens]

75
00:05:01.218 --> 00:05:03.468
[Ani] <i>There are things</i>
<i>I'm sure no one has told you.</i>

76
00:05:04.846 --> 00:05:06.596
<i>Secrets that have been well-kept.</i>

77
00:05:11.645 --> 00:05:15.515
<i>And yes. the keeper of those secrets
is often Clay Jensen.</i>

78
00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:17.027
[engine starting]

79
00:05:19.194 --> 00:05:20.534
[cell phone vibrating]

80
00:05:28.245 --> 00:05:29.245
Do you mind?

81
00:05:33.959 --> 00:05:36.089
[Ani] <i>One secret goes back to last spring.</i>

82
00:05:39.297 --> 00:05:41.547
- What the hell do you want. Jess?
- The cops took Clay.

83
00:05:41.633 --> 00:05:44.723
They perp-walked him out of school.
Ani saw just now.

84
00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:45.845
Shit!

85
00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:48.814
Do you think they know...

86
00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:50.349
about...

87
00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:52.980
- Tyler?
- Do you think so?

88
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.720
- Did you tell them?
- [scoffs] Are you fucking serious?

89
00:05:55.772 --> 00:05:57.932
- No. of course I didn't tell them.
- Really? 'Cause...

90
00:05:57.983 --> 00:06:00.153
you've been pretty hostile
to everyone lately.

91
00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:02.275
No. I've been pretty hostile
to you lately.

92
00:06:02.946 --> 00:06:05.049
Plus this whole Tyler thing happened
seven months ago.

93
00:06:05.073 --> 00:06:07.783
- Why would I say anything now?
- Why else would they want Clay?

94
00:06:08.535 --> 00:06:11.195
- How would I know?
- Did something happen this weekend?

95
00:06:11.746 --> 00:06:13.866
What did you do
after the homecoming game?

96
00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.211
Not very damn much.

97
00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:17.924
[bell rings]

98
00:06:19.462 --> 00:06:21.302
- Zach.
- I...

99
00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:23.299
have to go to history.

100
00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:27.104
[Ani] <i>These kids were connected</i>
<i>by their secrets.</i>

101
00:06:29.472 --> 00:06:31.562
<i>Connected and forever changed.</i>

102
00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:36.688
[Alex] Here. I'll help you with that.
in terms of ironic things happening.

103
00:06:36.855 --> 00:06:38.725
Not my first time on crutches. Alex.

104
00:06:38.815 --> 00:06:40.535
- C'mon. Zach. give me a win.
- [Jess] Alex?

105
00:06:42.444 --> 00:06:43.614
The cops were just here.

106
00:06:44.154 --> 00:06:46.034
- They took Clay in.
- Okay.

107
00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:47.737
- Okay?
- Yeah. I mean.

108
00:06:47.824 --> 00:06:49.624
Clay's not gonna say anything
about anybody.

109
00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.411
- Jess. come on.
- I have to go.

110
00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.754
What's up with her? Hasn't it been
a few months since you guys...

111
00:06:56.833 --> 00:07:00.593
Yeah. I guess it's a quick slide
from "we can be friends"

112
00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:02.130
to "don't fucking touch me."

113
00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:05.303
Your knee seems worse today.

114
00:07:05.717 --> 00:07:08.927
Friday night you could put some weight
on it. right? Without the crutches?

115
00:07:09.054 --> 00:07:10.604
Yeah. I mean...

116
00:07:11.306 --> 00:07:12.716
that's how these things go.

117
00:07:13.642 --> 00:07:14.642
It swells up.

118
00:07:16.978 --> 00:07:18.228
Your eye's looking worse.

119
00:07:18.939 --> 00:07:21.689
Yeah. that's the problem
with fighting football players.

120
00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:24.105
it's like they... they have helmets.

121
00:07:25.612 --> 00:07:28.242
[Ani] <i>Even the ones</i>
<i>that don't like each other that much.</i>

122
00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.115
<i>there's a bond.</i>

123
00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.452
<i>They show up for each other.</i>

124
00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.410
- Good morning.
- The cops took Clay.

125
00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.150
This morning. right outta school.

126
00:07:37.207 --> 00:07:38.207
The sheriffs?

127
00:07:39.542 --> 00:07:41.742
Javi. I gotta take care of something
for an hour or two.

128
00:07:41.795 --> 00:07:43.564
<i>- </i>[Javi] <i>Esta bien.</i>
- You can't go down there.

129
00:07:43.588 --> 00:07:44.588
You got a better idea?

130
00:07:44.673 --> 00:07:47.803
You can't go down there.
It's not a good idea for you. I'll go.

131
00:07:47.884 --> 00:07:49.554
You go down there. That's a better idea.

132
00:07:49.636 --> 00:07:51.906
- What about the guns?
- That's dealt with. You know that.

133
00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.270
No. all I know is you and Clay said
you took care of it.

134
00:07:54.349 --> 00:07:55.679
It's best that's all you know.

135
00:07:59.896 --> 00:08:01.016
[cell phone vibrating]

136
00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:03.569
[Ani] <i>So. yeah. The story begins</i>
<i>back in April.</i>

137
00:08:04.776 --> 00:08:07.236
<i>I mean. if we're going to understand
how we got here.</i>

138
00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:12.025
I'll be there in two minutes.

139
00:08:12.617 --> 00:08:13.617
I'm free and clear.

140
00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.660
I don't even think they looked
as I drove by.

141
00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:18.205
Yeah. Justin and those guys
are gonna talk to the police.

142
00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:19.419
We got a story.

143
00:08:19.541 --> 00:08:22.751
We didn't take it as real.
It's just him. you know?

144
00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:25.416
I heard him talking about it
and I jumped to conclusions.

145
00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.545
- It was a total joke. all right?
- [man] Yeah?

146
00:08:27.632 --> 00:08:29.472
It was fucking stupid
but it was a total joke.

147
00:08:29.551 --> 00:08:31.031
- [Standall] You made a joke?
- I did.

148
00:08:36.307 --> 00:08:37.977
[Tony] Tyler? How you doing?

149
00:08:39.436 --> 00:08:42.146
Just breathe. man.
Everything's going to be okay.

150
00:08:42.772 --> 00:08:44.322
[police sirens]

151
00:08:44.482 --> 00:08:48.532
Wait. they're... They're not coming here.
They're going to the school.

152
00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:52.162
But we need you
to get out of the backpack

153
00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:53.240
and the belt.

154
00:08:54.951 --> 00:08:58.081
I need you to be here... with me.

155
00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:01.923
- No. don't touch me!
- Okay!

156
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.420
- Don't fucking touch me!
- Okay. Tyler! I'm not.

157
00:09:06.046 --> 00:09:07.586
I'm over here. You're good.

158
00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:09.971
But I'm gonna need you
to take off the backpack

159
00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.180
and take off the belt

160
00:09:11.259 --> 00:09:12.679
and walk away from them.

161
00:09:27.317 --> 00:09:28.397
[Tony] Now walk towards me.

162
00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.070
It's just Clay.

163
00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:34.953
It's just Clay. see?

164
00:09:35.075 --> 00:09:37.655
I told you we were going to meet up
with him in the car.

165
00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:39.581
Right. Okay.

166
00:09:48.296 --> 00:09:49.296
[Clay] Hey. Tyler.

167
00:09:49.839 --> 00:09:50.839
How you doing?

168
00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:52.884
Shall we get you home?

169
00:09:56.346 --> 00:09:57.346
[Tyler] Oh. my God...

170
00:09:58.014 --> 00:09:59.014
My parents...

171
00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:01.350
Tyler...

172
00:10:02.727 --> 00:10:03.767
[Clay] What did you do?

173
00:10:04.896 --> 00:10:07.516
[Ani] <i>I don't know everything</i>
<i>that's happened since that night.</i>

174
00:10:08.858 --> 00:10:11.738
<i>but I know it was Bryce Walker's
last night at Liberty.</i>

175
00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:15.123
<i>And I'm the new kid. right?</i>

176
00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:18.201
<i>I watch. I listen.</i>

177
00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:20.619
<i>I know quite a bit.</i>

178
00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:25.174
<i>And I'll tell you everything.</i>

179
00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.960
Do I need a lawyer?

180
00:10:31.005 --> 00:10:32.715
[laughs] Oh... No.

181
00:10:34.551 --> 00:10:37.051
No. this isn't any kind
of criminal investigation.

182
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.390
And you're over 18 now. right?

183
00:10:41.516 --> 00:10:42.556
As of last month.

184
00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:44.602
Yeah. so you don't even
need a parent here.

185
00:10:45.145 --> 00:10:47.435
I mean. feel free to call your mom
if you want.

186
00:10:47.981 --> 00:10:49.321
No. Thank you.

187
00:10:49.941 --> 00:10:51.421
So. how are things at Liberty lately?

188
00:10:52.443 --> 00:10:53.533
Fine. I guess.

189
00:10:53.611 --> 00:10:56.661
Pretty stressful though. I imagine.
with everything that's going on.

190
00:10:57.907 --> 00:10:59.867
Hannah's trial. then Bryce.

191
00:11:00.368 --> 00:11:02.618
Then the false alarm
at the dance last spring.

192
00:11:02.704 --> 00:11:04.214
now all this at Homecoming.

193
00:11:04.998 --> 00:11:06.958
More than any one high school deserves.

194
00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:09.711
I think a lot of high schools
go through a lot worse.

195
00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:12.094
You're right.
But this thing with Homecoming...

196
00:11:13.047 --> 00:11:14.047
were you there?

197
00:11:14.465 --> 00:11:16.045
At the game Friday night?

198
00:11:16.426 --> 00:11:17.426
I was.

199
00:11:17.468 --> 00:11:18.718
Did you get caught up in it?

200
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:21.264
Not so much. A little.

201
00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:23.181
Did you run into Bryce Walker?

202
00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.060
We said hello.

203
00:11:25.143 --> 00:11:27.443
Okay. Was this before the game or after?

204
00:11:27.812 --> 00:11:28.812
Before.

205
00:11:30.565 --> 00:11:31.565
Why?

206
00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:33.355
Well...

207
00:11:33.526 --> 00:11:34.526
[sighing]

208
00:11:35.153 --> 00:11:37.533
See. the thing is. Clay...

209
00:11:39.449 --> 00:11:41.829
Bryce was playing for Hillcrest
on Friday night.

210
00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.080
He walked off the field
and hasn't been seen since.

211
00:11:48.124 --> 00:11:51.294
Do you have any idea where he could be
or who he could be with?

212
00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:58.050
[stammers] I don't.

213
00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:00.385
Hmm.

214
00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:04.679
Except for...

215
00:12:07.101 --> 00:12:08.271
we found this...

216
00:12:09.103 --> 00:12:10.613
inside Bryce's room.

217
00:12:11.189 --> 00:12:12.479
You recognize that?

218
00:12:15.902 --> 00:12:17.992
- [stammers] It used to be mine.
- You have any idea

219
00:12:18.071 --> 00:12:20.741
how Bryce could come to have it
or why would it be in his room?

220
00:12:21.824 --> 00:12:22.664
I don't know.

221
00:12:22.742 --> 00:12:25.372
When's the last time you saw it
or had it in your possession?

222
00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:30.380
[stammers] I don't remember.
I don't ride a bike anymore.

223
00:12:30.458 --> 00:12:31.458
Okay.

224
00:12:32.877 --> 00:12:33.877
Um...

225
00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.757
Clay. you were seen
outside of Bryce's house

226
00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.759
a few days before the homecoming game.

227
00:12:39.884 --> 00:12:42.644
You apparently threatened him.

228
00:12:47.684 --> 00:12:49.024
Specifically you said.

229
00:12:49.644 --> 00:12:50.854
"I'll fucking kill you."

230
00:12:52.063 --> 00:12:53.193
Can you explain that?

231
00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:56.820
Who told you that?

232
00:12:56.901 --> 00:12:59.031
It's not important.
Do you remember saying that?

233
00:12:59.946 --> 00:13:02.986
I was... I was checking on a friend.

234
00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:04.656
their safety.

235
00:13:04.742 --> 00:13:07.202
I mean. Bryce has a history.

236
00:13:10.498 --> 00:13:12.738
- [male teacher]...a triangle...
- [cell phone vibrating]

237
00:13:13.042 --> 00:13:14.922
...by repeatedly removing

238
00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:17.963
the middle triangle
from each of the prior generations.

239
00:13:18.506 --> 00:13:21.426
the number of colored triangles increases

240
00:13:21.509 --> 00:13:22.839
by a factor of...?

241
00:13:23.928 --> 00:13:27.268
Triangle recursion by a factor of three.

242
00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:29.062
- Mr. Wood?
- [Mr. Wood] Yes?

243
00:13:29.309 --> 00:13:32.599
Would it be possible for me to run
to the robotics room for a few?

244
00:13:32.687 --> 00:13:35.567
I've just realized
I've left a battery overcharging

245
00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.438
and it's going to fry the motherboard.

