00:27:22.933 --> 00:27:24.943
What night at his house last spring?

494
00:27:25.018 --> 00:27:26.308
Does Justin seem...

495
00:27:27.312 --> 00:27:28.312
freaked out?

496
00:27:31.441 --> 00:27:32.441
Aren't you?

497
00:27:35.821 --> 00:27:39.871
You don't have to worry about me. okay?
I can take care of myself.

498
00:27:56.758 --> 00:27:57.758
Hey. Alex.

499
00:27:58.051 --> 00:28:00.141
- Hey. did anyone text you?
- No. Why?

500
00:28:00.220 --> 00:28:01.220
Oh. shit.

501
00:28:01.513 --> 00:28:04.393
Sorry. I forgot you weren't
on the chain. It wasn't about you.

502
00:28:05.392 --> 00:28:06.392
Um...

503
00:28:06.476 --> 00:28:07.636
What was it about then?

504
00:28:08.854 --> 00:28:10.734
I guess Bryce Walker is missing.

505
00:28:12.941 --> 00:28:13.941
What does that mean?

506
00:28:14.484 --> 00:28:16.454
It means no one's seen him
since Friday night.

507
00:28:16.528 --> 00:28:18.528
But. like. do they think
something happened to him?

508
00:28:19.156 --> 00:28:20.276
I mean. who knows?

509
00:28:21.074 --> 00:28:23.294
Look. Justin has work
and Clay is still downtown.

510
00:28:23.368 --> 00:28:25.948
- so Cyrus said he'd give you a ride home.
- Oh. okay.

511
00:28:27.706 --> 00:28:29.666
- Is that not okay?
- No. it's great.

512
00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.170
[stammers] I just...

513
00:28:33.045 --> 00:28:35.705
He's probably not happy about it. right?

514
00:28:36.882 --> 00:28:39.552
Look. my mom's coming to get me later.
Do you want to wait with me?

515
00:28:40.802 --> 00:28:43.352
- Would that be okay?
- Yeah. Yeah.

516
00:28:43.722 --> 00:28:44.722
Out front at five.

517
00:28:45.265 --> 00:28:46.265
Okay.

518
00:29:06.620 --> 00:29:08.040
[zipping]

519
00:29:12.542 --> 00:29:15.052
[Ani] <i>When Bryce went missing. at first.</i>

520
00:29:15.128 --> 00:29:17.258
<i>we all figured he'd show up in time.</i>

521
00:29:18.131 --> 00:29:20.131
<i>We weren't really that worried about it.</i>

522
00:29:20.217 --> 00:29:21.887
I've missed the carriage house.

523
00:29:23.011 --> 00:29:25.061
Justin and I prefer "outhouse."

524
00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.983
Well. you two have done
some more decorating.

525
00:29:39.319 --> 00:29:40.319
We've not.

526
00:29:40.821 --> 00:29:42.451
Well. that wasn't there before.

527
00:29:42.948 --> 00:29:43.948
Or that.

528
00:29:45.784 --> 00:29:48.004
That's not decorating.
that's putting shit up.

529
00:29:48.078 --> 00:29:51.328
I apologize.
I should have used a more manly verb.

530
00:29:52.207 --> 00:29:53.207
I'm just saying.

531
00:29:53.750 --> 00:29:55.460
You are good at so many things.

532
00:29:55.544 --> 00:29:58.014
but one of your greatest gifts
is staying angry.

533
00:29:59.006 --> 00:30:00.006
I'm not angry with you.

534
00:30:00.299 --> 00:30:02.839
And self-awareness. not one of your gifts.

535
00:30:02.926 --> 00:30:06.306
I know myself just fine. I spend more time
in my own head than anywhere else.

536
00:30:06.388 --> 00:30:07.388
[scoffs] Breaking news!

537
00:30:11.727 --> 00:30:13.307
He's just gonna turn up. right?

538
00:30:14.479 --> 00:30:16.519
- Bryce?
- And what if he doesn't?

539
00:30:16.606 --> 00:30:18.896
And what if they find out
what happened at Homecoming?

540
00:30:18.984 --> 00:30:22.204
- So I lay low for a while.
- Clay. they arrested you.

541
00:30:22.279 --> 00:30:25.174
- Not yet. they just questioned me.
- Because they think you did something.

542
00:30:25.198 --> 00:30:27.738
- I didn't.
- Then shouldn't we find out who did?

543
00:30:27.826 --> 00:30:29.446
How did Bryce get my bike lock?

544
00:30:37.627 --> 00:30:38.627
[door opening]

545
00:30:39.629 --> 00:30:43.549
Day-old pastries.
I got us the Monday mother lode. Hey. Ani.

546
00:30:44.343 --> 00:30:45.223
[Justin groaning]

547
00:30:45.302 --> 00:30:47.722
[Justin] I have lemon bars. pound cake.

548
00:30:47.804 --> 00:30:50.314
scones so dry
they taste like you're eating a wall.

549
00:30:50.849 --> 00:30:52.389
- Oh. I love those.
- [Justin] Mmm.

550
00:30:53.101 --> 00:30:54.811
- I need some air.
- Clay...

551
00:30:59.066 --> 00:31:00.146
[whispering in Swahili]

552
00:31:09.618 --> 00:31:10.618
[door closing]

553
00:31:11.995 --> 00:31:13.635
Fucking hate when you guys speak African.

554
00:31:14.664 --> 00:31:18.714
Eh. you are aware that Africa is
an entire continent. yeah?

555
00:31:19.252 --> 00:31:22.132
- Yeah. I'm aware. Eat these.
- Hmm.

556
00:31:27.219 --> 00:31:28.219
[knock on door]

557
00:31:30.138 --> 00:31:31.308
- Hey. buddy.
- Hey. Dad.

558
00:31:31.681 --> 00:31:32.681
You got a minute?

559
00:31:33.266 --> 00:31:35.556
I want to talk to you
about some developments today.

560
00:31:35.644 --> 00:31:37.654
- Yeah.
- So... [sighing]

561
00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:39.480
Bryce Walker's missing.

562
00:31:39.523 --> 00:31:42.613
He hasn't been seen since
after the homecoming game Friday night.

563
00:31:42.692 --> 00:31:43.692
Oh. wow.

564
00:31:44.319 --> 00:31:46.739
- And Clay Jensen already told you.
- Yeah.

565
00:31:47.572 --> 00:31:49.412
Right. So. have you heard anything?

566
00:31:50.826 --> 00:31:51.826
Heard from Bryce?

567
00:31:52.369 --> 00:31:55.369
No. I mean.
I saw him real quick at the game.

568
00:31:55.455 --> 00:31:57.455
- but that was before it even started.
- All right.

569
00:31:58.959 --> 00:32:01.199
Didn't you two spend some time together
this past summer?

570
00:32:01.253 --> 00:32:02.343
Oh. I mean...

571
00:32:03.255 --> 00:32:05.965
a little. Not really.
I mean. it was a while ago.

572
00:32:06.758 --> 00:32:09.088
All right. Well. you know.
if you hear anything.

573
00:32:09.261 --> 00:32:12.061
We're hoping this kid's just missing
but his window's closing fast.

574
00:32:12.139 --> 00:32:14.929
Yeah. I'll let you know. Dad.
If I hear anything.

575
00:32:15.016 --> 00:32:16.016
All right.

576
00:32:17.227 --> 00:32:18.227
Hmm.

577
00:32:23.275 --> 00:32:24.355
[sighs]

578
00:32:35.120 --> 00:32:36.200
[Ani]<i> Where was Bryce?</i>

579
00:32:38.540 --> 00:32:39.750
<i>Had something happened?</i>

580
00:32:45.547 --> 00:32:48.757
<i>Did it have anything to do
with the secrets Clay Jensen had kept</i>

581
00:32:48.842 --> 00:32:50.222
<i>since that day last spring?</i>

582
00:32:53.346 --> 00:32:54.716
Yeah. it was a whole thing.

583
00:32:55.056 --> 00:32:57.016
At least you're all safe.

584
00:32:57.309 --> 00:32:59.479
It sounds like it was an overreaction.

585
00:33:03.231 --> 00:33:04.571
Okay. here you go. Justin.

586
00:33:04.649 --> 00:33:07.279
- So. the social worker visits a few times.
- [message alert]

587
00:33:07.360 --> 00:33:09.110
They process the paperwork.

588
00:33:09.196 --> 00:33:13.156
then they'll schedule the custody hearing
once everything's been filed

589
00:33:13.241 --> 00:33:15.621
and they've confirmed
that they can't contact your mother.

590
00:33:16.828 --> 00:33:17.948
Okay. Got it.

591
00:33:19.372 --> 00:33:22.382
Hey. I think we should
clear out the workshop.

592
00:33:22.667 --> 00:33:24.627
- Turn it into a bedroom.
- For Justin?

593
00:33:25.170 --> 00:33:27.890
So we bring him into the house
then send him to a different building?

594
00:33:27.923 --> 00:33:30.433
For both boys.
They're going to be seniors next year.

595
00:33:30.509 --> 00:33:32.509
- They need their space.
- [Clay's mom] Apparently.

596
00:33:32.552 --> 00:33:33.672
they don't need their space.

597
00:33:33.720 --> 00:33:37.180
as they manage all kinds
of miscreant behavior without us knowing.

598
00:33:38.099 --> 00:33:39.099
Right. Clay?

599
00:33:40.685 --> 00:33:41.685
Clay?

600
00:33:44.105 --> 00:33:45.105
Uh. right.

601
00:33:46.900 --> 00:33:47.980
[message alert]

602
00:33:51.780 --> 00:33:53.070
- Good morning. Tony.
- Morning.

603
00:33:53.156 --> 00:33:55.826
- Thanks for giving Tyler a ride.
- It's my pleasure.

604
00:33:58.620 --> 00:34:00.710
- You have a good one. Mrs. Down.
- You too.

605
00:34:00.789 --> 00:34:01.789
Bye.

606
00:34:10.257 --> 00:34:11.797
It's not really your pleasure.

607
00:34:12.467 --> 00:34:13.467
To drive me.

608
00:34:13.802 --> 00:34:14.802
Yeah. it is.

609
00:34:16.054 --> 00:34:17.064
I help my friends.

610
00:34:18.390 --> 00:34:19.390
I'm not your friend.

611
00:34:20.100 --> 00:34:21.100
Yeah. you are.

612
00:34:21.560 --> 00:34:23.900
Well. you're Clay's friend. clearly. so...

613
00:34:25.647 --> 00:34:26.647
you're mine.

614
00:34:29.818 --> 00:34:31.858
You think everyone will keep it secret?

615
00:34:32.654 --> 00:34:33.654
I do.

616
00:34:34.990 --> 00:34:36.450
We're all in this together.

617
00:34:37.325 --> 00:34:38.445
Who called the police?

618
00:34:39.786 --> 00:34:40.786
We don't know.

619
00:34:55.885 --> 00:34:56.965
[Ani]<i> Even knowing nothing.</i>

620
00:34:58.096 --> 00:35:00.176
<i>I could tell Clay had a lot going on.</i>

621
00:35:01.516 --> 00:35:02.886
<i>A lot to take care of.</i>

622
00:35:03.435 --> 00:35:05.265
[Monty] Hey. Tyler. What's up?

623
00:35:12.986 --> 00:35:16.356
[stammering] I can't... I can't do this.
I've got to go.

624
00:35:16.448 --> 00:35:18.448
Fuck that guy. He's not gonna hurt you.

625
00:35:18.908 --> 00:35:20.788
No one's gonna push you around anymore.

626
00:35:21.995 --> 00:35:24.285
- I can't.
- Tyler. it's okay.

627
00:35:25.165 --> 00:35:27.625
[Tony] Okay. Tyler.
I need you to listen to me. okay?

628
00:35:27.709 --> 00:35:29.209
Focus on your breathing. Hey.

629
00:35:30.837 --> 00:35:32.297
Breathe as deep as you can.

630
00:35:32.964 --> 00:35:34.094
[exhales deeply]

631
00:35:36.134 --> 00:35:38.184
Look. you have first with Alex. right?

632
00:35:38.261 --> 00:35:41.561
Stick with Alex. he'll walk you to second.
Me and Justin will meet you at lunch.

633
00:35:42.390 --> 00:35:44.180
Okay. Okay.

634
00:35:55.111 --> 00:35:57.951
Something happened to that kid.
He's not right.

635
00:35:58.657 --> 00:35:59.697
You think Monty...

636
00:36:00.283 --> 00:36:04.333
Well. Monty. Bryce. Jamie Garrison.
the kid gets it from fucking everywhere.

637
00:36:05.413 --> 00:36:06.923
There's no way this is gonna work.

638
00:36:09.042 --> 00:36:11.752
- It has to.
- Are you guys sure you got all his guns?

639
00:36:14.297 --> 00:36:17.217
[Ani] <i>The whole school was wired. on edge.</i>

640
00:36:17.300 --> 00:36:20.890
There will be an active shooter drill
some time in the next two weeks.

641
00:36:20.970 --> 00:36:22.810
We will not be told in advance.

642
00:36:23.056 --> 00:36:26.766
We don't want to add to anyone's anxiety
after Saturday's false alarm.

643
00:36:29.521 --> 00:36:30.521
Clay Jensen.

644
00:36:31.189 --> 00:36:32.269
Principal Bolan.

645
00:36:43.410 --> 00:36:46.080
- Hey. Clay.
- Hey. Courtney.

646
00:36:46.371 --> 00:36:49.016
- Sorry to pull you out of class.
- I thought it was Principal Bolan.

647
00:36:49.040 --> 00:36:51.790
I just used one of his slips.
It's our turn for the new student tour.

648
00:36:51.876 --> 00:36:53.956
I have an appointment
in the careers center

649
00:36:54.045 --> 00:36:56.875
and the Wellesley recruiter's
only here for a day. So. can you take it?

650
00:36:57.215 --> 00:36:58.585
Thank you! Thank you.

651
00:36:59.467 --> 00:37:01.427
Ani. it was nice to meet you.

652
00:37:01.511 --> 00:37:03.641
- You too. Bye.
- Goodbye. Thank you.

653
00:37:05.515 --> 00:37:06.925
You gotta be fucking kidding me?

654
00:37:08.309 --> 00:37:10.269
I don't really need a tour.

655
00:37:11.938 --> 00:37:13.688
[Clay] This is the trophy case.

656
00:37:13.773 --> 00:37:17.573
And we actually have many more
academic decathlon and robotics trophies.

657
00:37:17.652 --> 00:37:19.612
but they're kept
in the math and science wing.

658
00:37:19.696 --> 00:37:21.106
which is in a different building

659
00:37:21.573 --> 00:37:23.703
to keep the main student body
from being infected

660
00:37:23.783 --> 00:37:25.703
by something like actual knowledge.

661
00:37:25.785 --> 00:37:30.245
To your left is the classroom
of the ironically named Mr. Champion.

662
00:37:30.331 --> 00:37:33.421
who stares at girls' breasts
while he's talking to them.

663
00:37:33.501 --> 00:37:35.211
These are posters for the drama club.

664
00:37:35.295 --> 00:37:38.045
We actually have
the most low-key drama club anywhere.

665
00:37:38.131 --> 00:37:40.261
They're totally not annoying people
at all.

666
00:37:40.800 --> 00:37:43.180
The drawback being
their plays are super boring. but

667
00:37:43.553 --> 00:37:44.723
really nice people

668
00:37:44.804 --> 00:37:46.264
Library's out that way.

669
00:37:46.723 --> 00:37:48.183
It's a pretty typical library

670
00:37:48.266 --> 00:37:51.226
as high school libraries go.
which means underfunded

671
00:37:51.311 --> 00:37:54.271
and thoroughly devoid of any book
that could be remotely controversial.

672
00:37:54.355 --> 00:37:57.315
This is my locker.
which I sometimes use

673
00:37:57.400 --> 00:37:59.190
to stick my head into and scream.

674
00:37:59.903 --> 00:38:02.613
What the fuck?
Hey. leave him the fuck alone!

675
00:38:02.697 --> 00:38:05.487
Hey. I need you to step off
and leave him alone. got it?

676
00:38:05.909 --> 00:38:06.909
Dude. that's my brother.

677
00:38:07.994 --> 00:38:09.164
Oh. Um...

678
00:38:09.829 --> 00:38:12.499
Well. so the fuck what?
You should still leave him alone.

679
00:38:12.582 --> 00:38:14.182
Brothers should take care of each other.

680
00:38:18.922 --> 00:38:21.132
I told him no coffee before the tour.
but...

681
00:38:22.383 --> 00:38:26.973
They call this the back quad.
even though there's no front quad

682
00:38:27.055 --> 00:38:29.215
and back quad sounds like "backwad."

683
00:38:29.307 --> 00:38:31.307
which sounds either like a wedgie

684
00:38:31.392 --> 00:38:34.102
or a roll of fat that shows
when your shirt rides up.

685
00:38:34.896 --> 00:38:36.936
Football and soccer field down there.

686
00:38:37.398 --> 00:38:38.898
baseball field out there.

687
00:38:39.609 --> 00:38:41.609
Clearly the nicest parts of the school.

688
00:38:41.694 --> 00:38:45.664
because athletes are our heroes
and deserving of everything they want.

689
00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:47.740
including the ability
to sexually assault girls

690
00:38:47.826 --> 00:38:51.036
and never suffer any sort of consequences.
because why should they?

691
00:38:53.957 --> 00:38:54.957
Um...

692
00:38:55.416 --> 00:38:56.416
Sorry.

693
00:38:58.169 --> 00:39:01.259
Cafeteria over there. I bring my lunch.

694
00:39:01.798 --> 00:39:03.968
That's not a commentary
on the cafeteria food.

695
00:39:04.050 --> 00:39:06.760
that's just a nugget from my life.

696
00:39:08.221 --> 00:39:09.311
Wow.

697
00:39:09.514 --> 00:39:12.854
I've been to. like. five high schools
in three years.

698
00:39:13.643 --> 00:39:16.863
and that is by far the worst tour
I've ever been given.

699
00:39:17.230 --> 00:39:18.480
The absolute worst.

700
00:39:20.316 --> 00:39:21.776
[sighs] I'm sorry.

701
00:39:22.819 --> 00:39:24.569
It's kind of a weird time here.

702
00:39:25.864 --> 00:39:27.244
That's quite all right.

703
00:39:27.991 --> 00:39:30.031
It's also. like. my favorite tour ever.

704
00:39:31.786 --> 00:39:32.786
Well...

705
00:39:33.037 --> 00:39:34.037
thanks.

706
00:39:35.290 --> 00:39:36.330
[Ani] <i>He gave me a tour.</i>

707
00:39:37.125 --> 00:39:39.085
<i>Just a boring tour.</i>

708
00:39:41.838 --> 00:39:43.588
<i>I didn't really talk to him after.</i>

709
00:39:46.634 --> 00:39:49.304
Hey. You don't mind if I join. do you?

710
00:39:49.846 --> 00:39:51.806
I feel like you're obligated
to be nice to me.

711
00:39:51.890 --> 00:39:54.034
- at least for the rest of the day.
- Because you're new?

712
00:39:54.058 --> 00:39:56.978
Or because on my tour
you assaulted a guy.

713
00:39:59.105 --> 00:39:59.935
Ah...

714
00:40:00.023 --> 00:40:01.023
sure. have a seat.

715
00:40:03.026 --> 00:40:04.186
Hi. Ani.

716
00:40:05.486 --> 00:40:07.406
- Tyler.
- It's a pleasure. Tyler.

717
00:40:08.323 --> 00:40:09.663
So. tell me about Clay.

718
00:40:09.741 --> 00:40:12.491
He internalizes. doesn't he?

719
00:40:13.661 --> 00:40:14.751
Oh. I mean. I don't...

720
00:40:14.829 --> 00:40:17.329
You literally just met me.
How would you know that?

721
00:40:19.334 --> 00:40:20.334
Hey.

722
00:40:20.710 --> 00:40:23.170
Justin. Ani. Ani. Justin.

723
00:40:23.254 --> 00:40:24.254
Pleasure.

724
00:40:24.756 --> 00:40:27.426
You know. for a sour puss.
you have loads of friends.

725
00:40:28.509 --> 00:40:31.389
Tyler is my friend.
Justin lives with me and my family.

726
00:40:31.471 --> 00:40:32.471
They're adopting me.

727
00:40:32.889 --> 00:40:34.019
Oh. that's fantastic.

728
00:40:34.223 --> 00:40:36.683
Clay believes brothers should
take care of each other.

729
00:40:36.976 --> 00:40:39.096
I need... ketchup.

730
00:40:42.982 --> 00:40:43.982
[clears throat]

731
00:40:44.734 --> 00:40:49.914
So. he might seem like an uptight asshole
at first. maybe even for a while.

732
00:40:50.698 --> 00:40:51.698
but...

733
00:40:52.533 --> 00:40:55.873
he's a really good guy.
so just give him some time. He's worth it.

734
00:40:57.372 --> 00:40:58.372
How much time?

735
00:40:58.665 --> 00:40:59.665
Hmm.

736
00:40:59.707 --> 00:41:01.827
For me. it took. like. eight years. but...

737
00:41:04.003 --> 00:41:05.593
[Ani] <i>I thought Clay was funny.</i>

738
00:41:06.130 --> 00:41:07.380
<i>but not much beyond that.</i>

739
00:41:08.508 --> 00:41:10.508
<i>His friend Jessica was more interesting.</i>

740
00:41:10.593 --> 00:41:13.393
[Courtney] Principal Bolan is just asking
that we do something.

741
00:41:13.471 --> 00:41:16.721
